---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import { SITE_DESCRIPTION, SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title="Foo HeanTee | Identity & Access Security Engineer" description="Personal site of Foo HeanTee, a cybersecurity engineer with 20 years in IT. Notes on IAM, PAM, Microsoft Entra ID, and homelab projects." />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
		<em><h4><code>foo</code> <em>(noun) </em>: A temporary placeholder, or just my actual surname.</h4></em>
    	<h1>Hi, I’m Foo: an identity and cybersecurity engineer.</h1>
    	<p>Yes, that’s my real surname. Yes, I’m also a tech person. No, it’s not a placeholder.</p>
    	<p>When your surname is Foo, there’s really only one thing to do: register it as a domain. So I did.</p>
   	 <p>Pretty cool, ya? 😎</p>	
	 <h3>What You’ll Find Here</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>📝 <strong>Blog:</strong> Tech write-ups, lab experiments, and the occasional rabbit hole.</li>
        <li>🖥️ <strong>Homelab:</strong> A mini PC, some VMs, and a lot of "why is this not working?"</li>
        <li>📄 <strong>Résumé:</strong> The serious bit, for when you need proof I’m a real person.</li>
      </ul>
    
    
      <h3>What I Do</h3>
      <p>I work in cybersecurity and identity: focusing on who gets access to what, and how to keep the wrong people out.</p>
      <p>I’m here to learn, experiment, and document the journey. No guru status claimed. No promises that everything will work on the first try.</p>
      <p>Have a look around. You might find something useful.</p>
      <p>And if not, at least you’ve met someone who turned a surname into a domain.</p>

		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
